  "body": "Found during #3746.\n\n## What happens\n\n#3746 gives the Arc entry of a start-side pass (2D Offset, \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside round a part) a plunge in air outside the stock box and a G17 arc onto the first ring. The change is in `pocket_started_on` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket.rs`, `air_entry.rs`).\n\nThe avoid route (`pocket_avoid_started_on`, used when the op has fixtures or clamps to avoid) builds its own `Motion` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_avoid.rs`, near the `with_cleared_links` call). That `Motion` has no air room. Thus with fixtures, the Arc entry keeps the old behaviour: \"the arc's lead room is blocked - axial dive on the floor instead\". The dive is named, so it is not silent.\n\n## Why it was not done in #3746\n\nThe air outside the stock box is proved free only of the part. On the avoid route, a fixture or a clamp can stand outside the stock box. The air room must subtract the keep-outs of the avoid spec (grown by the tool radius) before a lead can use it.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The avoid route passes an `AirRoom` whose legal area is the cutter-centre area joined with the air outside the stock box, less each keep-out grown by the tool radius.\n- A pin on the dog-bone part with a clamp outside the stock box: the plunge stands outside the box by the tool radius plus the approach distance, and the lead does not touch the clamp.\n",
